    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="authoring" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Writing a page</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Create <code>src/pages/docs/&lt;slug&gt;.astro</code> using <code>DocsLayout</code> with <code>title</code>, <code>subtitle</code>, <code>description</code> and a <code>toc</code> array whose <code>href</code>s match section ids.</li>
      <li>Write each section as <code>&lt;section id="…" class="doc-section"&gt;</code> with one <code>&lt;h2&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li>Use <code>DocCode</code> (<code>language</code>, <code>title</code>) for code, <code>DocCallout</code> (<code>type</code> info, warn or note) for warnings, <code>DocCard</code> for link grids, <code>DocRelated</code> at the end, and <code>DocViewer3D</code> for 3D previews.</li>
      <li>Escape literal braces in text as <code>&amp;#123;</code> and <code>&amp;#125;</code>; put code inside an expression such as <code>&#123;String.raw`…`&#125;</code>.</li>
      <li>Add the page to the sidebar data and run <code>bun run typecheck</code>, which also rebuilds and checks the search index.</li>
    </ol>
    <DocCode language="astro" title="Minimal page">
{"---\nexport const prerender = true\nimport DocsLayout from \"../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro\"\nimport DocCode from \"../../components/docs/DocCode.astro\"\nconst toc = [{ title: \"Overview\", href: \"#overview\" }]\n---\n<DocsLayout title=\"Example\" subtitle=\"One line.\" description=\"For search engines.\" toc={toc}>\n  <section id=\"overview\" class=\"doc-section\">\n    <h2>Overview</h2>\n    <p>Text with an escaped brace: &#123;</p>\n    <DocCode language=\"bash\" title=\"Run\">{`bun run typecheck`}</DocCode>\n  </section>\n</DocsLayout>"}
    </DocCode>
    <DocCallout type="note" title="Verify every fact">
      <p>Only document behaviour you can point to in the code, and run examples before pasting their output. The API reference is generated; hand-written pages are not.</p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="viewer3d" class="doc-section">
    <h2>3D previews</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>title</code>, <code>caption</code></td><td>string</td><td>Heading and explanation under the canvas</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>solids</code></td><td>array</td><td><code>box</code> (<code>size</code>), <code>extrude</code> (<code>profile</code>, <code>holes</code>, <code>height</code>) or <code>cylinder</code> (<code>radius</code>, <code>height</code>), each with optional <code>at</code>, <code>color</code>, <code>opacity</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>paths</code></td><td>array</td><td>Polylines with <code>points</code> as [x, y, z], <code>rapid</code> (dashed) and <code>color</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>height</code></td><td>number</td><td>Canvas height in pixels</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>animate</code></td><td>boolean</td><td>Draw paths progressively and show a replay button</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>The component uses three.js with Z up, mounts only when scrolled into view and shows a text fallback without WebGL. Feed it real output, such as kernel moves, rather than hand-drawn coordinates.</p>
  </section>

